{# ============================================================================
   /insights/ — rebuilt 2026-08-27 to the client's reference layout: a photo
   masthead, a venture filter, one featured row, a 2-up grid for the rest.

   Things NOT carried over from the reference, on purpose:

   1. The reference's filter pills were 5 categories (All / Education /
      Careers / Exams / Global Opportunities) that don't match anything in
      the data — most would return zero or one result. Built instead as a
      REAL filter over the venture field every post already has: All +
      the 3 actual ventures, and every option returns a real result
      (CLAUDE.md non-negotiable #3 — interactivity must navigate real
      content, not decorate).
   2. The reference showed "8 MIN READ" on all three posts. That's not
      measured from anything — kept the real readingTime filter
      (.eleventy.js) instead, which computes it from actual word count.
      All three posts are short, so it genuinely reads "1 min read" — a
      true number, not a rounder-looking invented one.

   The 2-up grid uses `grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(...))`
   (main.css), not a fixed `repeat(2, ...)`. A fixed 2-column grid was tried
   first and reintroduced the exact bug this page shipped without earlier:
   filtering down to one visible card left its sibling's column empty.
   auto-fit collapses that empty track, so a single visible card fills the
   row — no JS counting needed, and the grid still reads as 2-up whenever
   both cards are visible (the reference's actual look, by default).

   Masthead photo (masthead-notes.jpg) is stock photography (Pexels
   License, free commercial use, no attribution required) — atmospheric
   only, not a real Admizz space, same basis as the /about/ and /ventures/
   photography exceptions.
   ============================================================================ #}

<section class="insights-masthead bg-paper">
  <div class="shell"><div class="page-canvas insights-masthead-grid">
    <div class="fade-up">
      <span class="eyebrow">Insights</span>
      <h1 class="mt-4 font-display font-light text-display-2 text-ink max-w-[14ch] text-balance">
        Ideas for what&rsquo;s <em class="italic text-navy font-book">next.</em>
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-5 text-body-lg text-ink-muted max-w-measure-tight leading-relaxed">
        Perspectives from across Admizz Education, Admizz Institute and Admizz Workforce Solutions.
      </p>

      {# 2026-09-08: the copy column ran out well above the photo's bottom
         edge, leaving a dead block of paper under it. Filled with something
         real rather than filler: the counts are computed from the actual
         data (no hardcoded "6"), and the sourcing line is only true because
         the research pieces genuinely cite primary sources — which is now
         the strongest thing this page can say about itself. #}
      <dl class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-8 gap-y-3">
        <div>
          <dt class="font-mono text-label uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-faint">Articles</dt>
          <dd class="mt-1 font-display font-light text-h3 text-ink tabular-nums">{{ insights | length }}</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="font-mono text-label uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-faint">Businesses</dt>
          <dd class="mt-1 font-display font-light text-h3 text-ink tabular-nums">{{ ventures | length }}</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="font-mono text-label uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-faint">Sourced research</dt>
          {# selectattr, not a {% set %} counter inside a {% for %} — a
             variable assigned inside a Nunjucks loop doesn't survive
             outside it, so that rendered blank (caught in the built
             output, not assumed). #}
          <dd class="mt-1 font-display font-light text-h3 text-ink tabular-nums">{{ insights | selectattr("citations") | length }}</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
      <p class="mt-5 text-small text-ink-muted max-w-measure-tight leading-relaxed">
        Pieces marked <span class="insights-tag-research">Research</span> cite third-party data, read at its primary source before publication &mdash; see <a href="/sources/" class="link-underline text-ink">Sources &amp; Methodology</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="insights-masthead-photo fade-up" style="animation-delay:80ms">
      {% imageEager "src/assets/images/insights/masthead-notes.jpg", "Someone writing out a plan by hand next to an open laptop", "(min-width: 900px) 42vw, 92vw" %}
    </div>
  </div></div>
</section>

<section class="bg-paper pb-section" x-data="{
    active: 'all',
    posts: {{ insights | pluck(["venture", "featured"]) | json }},
    get gridCount() {
      return this.posts.filter(p => !p.featured && (this.active === 'all' || this.active === p.venture)).length;
    }
  }">
  <div class="shell"><div class="page-canvas">
    {# Real filter — every option is a venture that actually has a post
       behind it; "All" plus the 3 real values, nothing invented. #}
    <div class="insights-filters fade-up" role="group" aria-label="Filter by venture">
      <button type="button" class="insights-filter-pill" :class="active === 'all' ? 'is-active' : ''" @click="active = 'all'">All</button>
      {% for v in ventures %}
      <button type="button" class="insights-filter-pill" :class="active === '{{ v.name }}' ? 'is-active' : ''" @click="active = '{{ v.name }}'">{{ v.name | replace("Admizz ", "") }}</button>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>

    {# Featured piece (2026-09-08 v2) — was a plain 2-column photo/text
       split. Rebuilt on the SaleUnion reference's signature layering
       move: the copy sits in a raised card pulled up over the bottom
       edge of its own image, so the two read as one composed object
       rather than a picture with a caption beside it. Falls back
       gracefully with no JS — the overlap is pure CSS margin. #}
    {% for post in insights %}{% if post.featured %}
    <article class="mt-10 fade-up" x-show="active === 'all' || active === '{{ post.venture }}'">
      <a href="/insights/{{ post.slug }}/" class="overlap-media" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
        {% image "src/assets/images/insights/" + post.image, post.imageAlt, "(min-width: 900px) 78vw, 92vw" %}
      </a>
      <div class="overlap-card">
        <span class="font-mono text-label uppercase tracking-widest text-gold-text">Featured</span>
        <h2 class="mt-3 font-display font-book text-h2 text-ink text-balance max-w-[22ch]">
          <a href="/insights/{{ post.slug }}/" class="hover:text-navy-soft transition-colors duration-press ease-signature">{{ post.title }}</a>
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-body text-ink-muted max-w-measure leading-relaxed">{{ post.deck }}</p>
        <div class="insights-row-foot mt-5">
          <a href="/insights/{{ post.slug }}/" class="text-small font-medium text-navy link-underline">Read the article &rarr;</a>
          <span class="insights-row-time">{{ post.venture }} &middot; {{ post.body | readingTime }} min read</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
    {% endif %}{% endfor %}

    {# Article mosaic (2026-09-08 v3) — was a uniform 2-up card grid, i.e.
       the layout every template ships with. Rebuilt as a bento: the first
       non-featured piece takes a wide photo cell, the rest are text cells,
       so the block has real hierarchy instead of five identical tiles.

       The empty-state and column behaviour still come from `gridCount`,
       computed in Alpine from the actual post data (see x-data above) —
       a previous version hardcoded which ventures had grid posts and broke
       the moment any venture had more than one. Not auto-fit either: that
       was tried and rejected (see .insights-grid's CSS note) because it
       also collapses on an ordinary narrow window, not just when filtered. #}
    {# rejectattr first: looping `insights` and skipping the featured post
       inside the loop left loop.index counting the skipped item too, so the
       photo cell landed on the wrong card. Iterating the filtered list makes
       the index mean what it reads as. #}
    {% set restPosts = insights | rejectattr("featured") %}
    <div class="bento mt-14" x-show="gridCount > 0">
      {% for post in restPosts %}
      {% set isPhoto = loop.index == 1 or loop.index == 4 %}
      <article
        class="bento-item {% if isPhoto %}bento-item-photo bento-wide{% elif post.citations %}bento-item-tint{% endif %} fade-up"
        style="animation-delay:{{ loop.index0 * 70 }}ms"
        x-show="active === 'all' || active === '{{ post.venture }}'">

        {% if isPhoto %}
        <div class="bento-photo-img" aria-hidden="true">
          {% image "src/assets/images/insights/" + post.image, post.imageAlt, "(min-width: 1000px) 40vw, 92vw" %}
        </div>
        <span class="bento-photo-scrim" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="journey-plate-badge bento-tag">{{ "0" }}{{ loop.index }} / {{ post.venture | replace("Admizz ", "") }}</span>
        <div class="bento-photo-body">
          {% if post.citations %}<span class="insights-tag-research insights-tag-research-on-navy">Research</span>{% endif %}
          <h2 class="mt-3 font-display font-book text-h3 text-navy-on text-balance max-w-[20ch]">
            <a href="/insights/{{ post.slug }}/" class="hover:text-navy-accent transition-colors duration-press ease-signature">{{ post.title }}</a>
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-2 text-small text-navy-on-muted max-w-measure-tight">{{ post.deck }}</p>
          <div class="mt-4 flex items-center gap-5">
            <a href="/insights/{{ post.slug }}/" class="text-small font-medium text-navy-on link-underline">Read the article &rarr;</a>
            {% if post.citations %}
            <span class="font-mono text-label uppercase tracking-widest text-navy-accent">{{ post.citations | length }} sources</span>
            {% else %}
            <span class="font-mono text-label uppercase tracking-widest text-navy-on-muted">{{ post.body | readingTime }} min read</span>
            {% endif %}
          </div>
        </div>

        {% else %}
        <div>
          <span class="font-mono text-label uppercase tracking-widest text-navy-soft">
            {{ post.venture | replace("Admizz ", "") }}{% if post.citations %} <span class="insights-tag-research">Research</span>{% endif %}
          </span>
          <h2 class="mt-3 font-display font-book text-h4 text-ink text-balance">
            <a href="/insights/{{ post.slug }}/" class="hover:text-navy-soft transition-colors duration-press ease-signature">{{ post.title }}</a>
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-2 text-small text-ink-muted">{{ post.deck }}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-5 flex items-center justify-between gap-4">
          <a href="/insights/{{ post.slug }}/" class="text-small font-medium text-navy link-underline">Read the article &rarr;</a>
          {# Marker driven by the post's real `citations` array — no
             hand-set flag to drift out of sync with the content. #}
          {% if post.citations %}
          <span class="insights-sourced">
            <svg width="11" height="11" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 3.5h10M2 7h10M2 10.5h6" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
            {{ post.citations | length }} sources
          </span>
          {% else %}
          <span class="insights-row-time">{{ post.body | readingTime }} min read</span>
          {% endif %}
        </div>
        {% endif %}
      </article>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div></div>
</section>

